2. The `loaded` mechanism holds on EVERY path                  => PASS
====================================================================
Mechanism read: internal/services/accounts/accounts.go:80-99 (Mutate). fn is
reached only after `s == nil` and loadTx both succeed; saveTx is reached only
after fn returns nil. `loaded = true` is the FIRST statement of every closure —
verified by `grep -n -A2 'accounts.Mutate(store, func(accts'`
(handlers.go:190/191, 259/260, 316/317) and
`grep -n -A2 'accounts.Mutate(deps.Store, func(accts'` (anchor.go:210/211).
`grep -n loaded` shows exactly four declare/set/test triples and no other use;
each `loaded` is a per-request local, read synchronously after Mutate returns
(Mutate never calls fn on another goroutine), so there is no shared-state hazard.
applyForm (handlers.go:451) deliberately has no `loaded` — correct per brief.

Enumeration, each confirmed by execution rather than reading (checker probe
staged and run ONLY in the scratch copy <scratch>/mut, never in the repo;
source kept at <scratch>/mut/internal/handlers/accounts/zz_checker_crit2_test.go):
  go test -count=1 -v -run 'TestZZCrit2' ./internal/handlers/accounts/
  --- PASS: TestZZCrit2_FnErrorIsNot500
        addAnchor missing-account status=404  (fn returns errAccountNotFound
        AFTER being called -> loaded=true -> 404, not the !loaded 500)
  --- PASS: TestZZCrit2_AnchorNotFoundIsNot500
        deleteAnchor missing-anchor status=404 (errAnchorNotFound, same)
  --- PASS: TestZZCrit2_SaveValidationFailureIsNot500
        saveTx-Validate-failure status=200 (duplicate IDs written raw so
        Validate trips inside saveTx, after a successful load -> 200 inline)
  --- PASS: TestZZCrit2_NilStorageMatchesHEAD
        nil-store status=500, body contains
        "Failed to load accounts: accounts: nil storage" — identical to what
        HEAD produced, since HEAD's accounts.Load(nil) returned that same
        string into the same renderError (asserted in the probe by calling
        accountssvc.Load(nil) and comparing).
  write failure  -> covered by the three SaveFailureStays200 tests above
                    (loaded=true, 200 inline).
CONCLUSION: the only two paths that leave `loaded` false are the nil-storage
guard and loadTx — neither is a save. No save/validation/write failure can
reach the 500 branch.

